START:
1. Make sure that you are in the virtual environment. `.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1`
2. Load the .env file into context `Get-Content .env | ForEach-Object { if ($_ -match '^([^=]+)=(.*)$') { [System.Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable($matches[1], $matches[2], 'Process') } }`

No piping commands with cat, they already have nice CLI interfaces.
Always aim to correct my understanding of the problem if I misunderstand anything.
We are both working on this together, so let's do our best together.
Actively make memories when working on this repo.
Always fix issues in this repo as we have ownership over it.